course: dictionary
lesson: 12548
title: Determined: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives «determined» three meanings, so look at the words around it to choose the right one. This is the context clue skill.
explain: The first meaning is about a person. «Maya was determined to finish the race, even when her legs ached.» Maya had firmly decided, and nothing would stop her.
explain: The other meanings are about finding out or deciding things, often in science and maths. «The winner was determined by the judges' scores.» Here, determined means decided by something else.
explain: To check your choice, swap your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have the right one.
fact: «Determined» means having decided firmly to do something and not letting anything stop you.
fact: «Determined» can also be the past form of «determine», which means find out exactly, as in «The cause was determined».
fact: In maths, «determine the value of x» means find the value of x.
fact: «Determined» can also mean decided or controlled by something, as in «Your height is partly determined by your genes».
fact: A person who keeps trying is determined; a result that was worked out is determined too, so check the context.
exercise: «Ella was determined to learn to swim, so she practised every day.» What does determined mean here? | Bored of the pool | *Having decided firmly and not giving up | Lost and confused | Sleepy after lunch
exercise: Mr Patel says, «Determine the total of these numbers.» What should you do? | Guess the first number | Draw a picture of the numbers | Hide the numbers | *Find the total
exercise: «The winner was determined by the judges' scores.» What does determined mean here? | Firmly set on winning | Very tired | Painted in bright colours | *Decided by the judges' scores
test: «The scientist was determined to repeat the experiment until the result was clear.» Which meaning fits best? | Forgotten and lost | *Firmly set on doing it and never giving up | Found out exactly by a rule | Painted red
test: «The flavour of the sweets is partly determined by the sugar.» What does determined mean here? | *Decided or controlled by something | Hidden under the table | Firmly set on eating them all | Finished and packed
exam: Which sentence uses determined to mean found out exactly? | Tom was determined to win the match | *The length of the table was determined by measuring it | Lucy was determined to become a doctor | The dog was determined to find its ball
